ESTIMAND := define_incremental_effect(budget_and_policy_changes, business_outcomes)
// Do not promise placement/query attribution; hidden platform decisions make that unidentifiable.
CONTROL_SURFACE := inventory(actions_we_can_randomize: budgets, eligibility, timing, objectives)
LEDGER := join(assignments, spend, platform_changes, pricing, inventory, server_side_outcomes)
// The outcome source and treatment log must be independent of platform attribution.
CELLS := choose_geo_time_or_audience_units_after_power_and_interference_simulation()
// If no design can detect the minimum useful effect, say so rather than manufacture precision.
ASSIGN := run_persistent_low_amplitude_factorial_encouragements(CONTROL_SURFACE, CELLS)
// Randomized nudges preserve learning better than long shutdowns, but adaptation and spillovers remain risks.
EFFECTS := estimate_intent_to_treat_and_IV(ASSIGN, actual_spend, outcomes)
// Measure marginal effects of controllable policies, not an imaginary decomposition of every conversion.
MODEL := fit_drift_aware_state_space_response(EFFECTS, ledger_covariates, partial_pooling)
// Use MMM to interpolate between experiments; never treat it as self-validating ground truth.
VALIDATE := preregister_out_of_sample_lift_predictions_and_score_across_repeated_tests()
REPORT := publish_bounds, sensitivity_to_spillovers, drift_flags, and explicit_non_identifiability

Hush now, join outcomes and spend, then randomize where we may;
With ghost ads, switchbacks, and small holds, gather shards along the way.

Let models borrow from those shards, but report bounds, not truth;
No prettier MMM can conjure missing proof.

Track every platform policy turn and let stale priors fall;
Build shared, blinded benchmark cases, judged by one rule for all.

We may narrow which ads caused the lift despite the data they hide;
But no song can prove each ad worked when platforms seal the inside.
